Vikram and Betal: The Clever Thief

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a thief who was very clever,” said Betal. “He never got caught.”

One day, he stole a bag of gold from a merchant.

The merchant went to the king and complained.

The king ordered his guards to catch the thief.

The thief knew he might be caught, so he made a plan.

He hid the gold under a tree and acted like an innocent man.

When the guards questioned him, he said, “I saw someone hiding something under that tree.”

The guards rushed to the tree and found the gold.

They thought the thief was telling the truth and let him go.

But a wise officer became suspicious.

He said, “Only the thief would know exactly where the gold is hidden.”

The guards caught the thief.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, how was the thief caught?”

Vikram replied, “Because his cleverness revealed the truth.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Wrong actions will always be revealed.
